{"id":"mahabharata-7-125","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":125,"title":"पञ्चविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 125 · Duryodhana's grief and reproach to Drona","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana, in tears at the fall of Jayadratha, goes to Drona and blames him for failing to protect the king while the Pandavas are not defeated. Drona answers, and Duryodhana says he has no wish to live without those who fell.","kn":"ಜಯದ್ರಥನ ಪತನದಿಂದ ಕಣ್ಣೀರಿಟ್ಟ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ದ್ರೋಣನ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗಿ ರಾಜನನ್ನು ಕಾಯಲಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ದೂಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಸೋಲಲಿಲ್ಲ. ದ್ರೋಣ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬಿದ್ದವರಿಲ್ಲದೆ ತನಗೆ ಬದುಕಲು ಇಷ್ಟವಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जयद्रथ के गिरने पर आँसू बहाता दुर्योधन द्रोण के पास जाकर उन्हें राजा की रक्षा न करने के लिए दोष देता है जबकि पाण्डव अजेय हैं। द्रोण उत्तर देते हैं, और दुर्योधन कहता है कि गिरे हुओं के बिना वह जीना नहीं चाहता।","te":"జయద్రథుని పతనంతో కన్నీళ్లతో దుర్యోధనుడు ద్రోణుని వద్దకు వెళ్లి రాజును కాపాడలేదని నిందిస్తాడు; పాండవులు ఓడలేదు. ద్రోణుడు బదులిస్తాడు; పడిపోయిన వారు లేకుండా తాను బతకదలచలేదని దుర్యోధనుడు అంటాడు.","ta":"ஜயத்ரதன் வீழ்ந்ததால் கண்ணீர் சிந்தும் துரியோதனன் த்ரோணரிடம் சென்று மன்னரைக் காக்கவில்லை என்று குறை கூறுகிறான்; பாண்டவர் வெல்லப்படவில்லை. த்ரோணர் பதிலளிக்க, வீழ்ந்தவர் இன்றி உயிர்வாழ விரும்பவில்லை என்கிறான் துரியோதனன்.","ml":"ജയദ്രഥന്റെ വീഴ്ചയിൽ കണ്ണീരോടെ ദുര്യോധനൻ ദ്രോണരുടെ അടുത്തെത്തി, പാണ്ഡവർ പരാജയപ്പെടാത്തപ്പോൾ രാജാവിനെ സംരക്ഷിക്കുന്നതിൽ പരാജയപ്പെട്ടതിന് അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കുറ്റപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു. ദ്രോണർ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; വീണുപോയവരില്ലാതെ ജീവിക്കാൻ തനിക്ക് ആഗ്രഹമില്ലെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.125; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सैन्धवे निहते राजन्पुत्रस्तव सुयोधनः ।\nअश्रुक्लिन्नमुखो दीनो निरुत्साहो द्विषज्जये ।\nअमन्यतार्जुनसमो योधो भुवि न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Saindhava was killed, O king, your son Suyodhana, his face wet with tears, dejected and without heart for conquering his foes, felt that no warrior on earth was Arjuna's equal."}},{"n":2,"text":"न द्रोणो न च राधेयो नाश्वत्थामा कृपो न च ।\nक्रुद्धस्य प्रमुखे स्थातुं पर्याप्ता इति मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thought that neither Drona, nor Radheya, nor Ashvatthama, nor Kripa was able to stand in front of Arjuna when he was angry."}},{"n":3,"text":"निर्जित्य हि रणे पार्थः सर्वान्मम महारथान् ।\nअवधीत्सैन्धवं संख्ये नैनं कश्चिदवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For Partha, having beaten all my great chariot-fighters in battle, killed Saindhava, and no one stopped him."}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वथा हतमेवैतत्कौरवाणां महद्बलम् ।\nन ह्यस्य विद्यते त्राता साक्षादपि पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great army of the Kauravas is altogether as good as dead; it has no protector, even if Indra himself were there."}},{"n":5,"text":"यमुपाश्रित्य संग्रामे कृतः शस्त्रसमुद्यमः ।\nस कर्णो निर्जितः संख्ये हतश्चैव जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, on whom I relied when I took up arms in this war, has been beaten in battle, and Jayadratha is dead."}},{"n":6,"text":"परुषाणि सभामध्ये प्रोक्तवान्यः स्म पाण्डवान् ।\nस कर्णो निर्जितः संख्ये सैन्धवश्च निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, who spoke harsh words to the Pandavas in the middle of the assembly, has been beaten, and Saindhava has been felled."}},{"n":7,"text":"यस्य वीर्यं समाश्रित्य शमं याचन्तमच्युतम् ।\nतृणवत्तमहं मन्ये स कर्णो निर्जितो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on whose strength I thought of Krishna, begging for peace, as a straw, that Karna has been beaten in battle.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एवं क्लान्तमना राजन्नुपायाद्द्रोणमीक्षितुम् ।\nआगस्कृत्सर्वलोकस्य पुत्रस्ते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, with a weary mind, O king, your son, the offender against the whole world, O best of the Bharatas, came to see Drona."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततस्तत्सर्वमाचख्यौ कुरूणां वैशसं महत् ।\nपरान्विजयतश्चापि धार्तराष्ट्रान्निमज्जतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he told him all of the great slaughter of the Kurus and how Dhritarashtra's sons, though winning, were sinking."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"पश्य मूर्धावसिक्तानामाचार्य कदनं कृतम् ।\nकृत्वा प्रमुखतः शूरं भीष्मं मम पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Teacher, look at the slaughter of anointed kings, and how, putting my grandfather, the hero Bhishma, in front,"}},{"n":11,"text":"तं निहत्य प्रलुब्धोऽयं शिखण्डी पूर्णमानसः ।\nपाञ्चालैः सहितः सर्वैः सेनाग्रमभिकर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"and killing him, greedy Shikhandi with satisfied heart drags the army's front along with all the Panchalas."}},{"n":12,"text":"अपरश्चापि दुर्धर्षः शिष्यस्ते सव्यसाचिना ।\nअक्षौहिणीः सप्त हत्वा हतो राजा जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And another, your unconquerable pupil, killed by Savyasachin seven akshauhinis and then King Jayadratha."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्मद्विजयकामानां सुहृदामुपकारिणाम् ।\nगन्तास्मि कथमानृण्यं गतानां यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For friends who benefit us and who wished us victory, and have gone to Yama's house, how shall I ever repay my debt?"}},{"n":14,"text":"ये मदर्थं परीप्सन्ति वसुधां वसुधाधिपाः ।\nते हित्वा वसुधैश्वर्यं वसुधामधिशेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings who tried to win the earth for my sake have left the earth's sovereignty and lie upon the earth."}},{"n":15,"text":"सोऽहं कापुरुषः कृत्वा मित्राणां क्षयमीदृशम् ।\nनाश्वमेधसहस्रेण पातुमात्मानमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a coward am I, who caused my friends' ruin like this, that I cannot cleanse myself even with a thousand horse sacrifices."}},{"n":16,"text":"मम लुब्धस्य पापस्य तथा धर्मापचायिनः ।\nव्यायच्छन्तो जिगीषन्तः प्राप्ता वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For me, a greedy sinner who offended against dharma, those who strove and wished to win have reached Vaivasvata's house."}},{"n":17,"text":"कथं पतितवृत्तस्य पृथिवी सुहृदां द्रुहः ।\nविवरं नाशकद्दातुं मम पार्थिवसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did the earth fail to open a crack for me in the assembly of kings, me of fallen conduct and a betrayer of friends?"}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽहं रुधिरसिक्ताङ्गं राज्ञां मध्ये पितामहम् ।\nशयानं नाशकं त्रातुं भीष्ममायोधने हतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I could not save my grandfather Bhishma, his body soaked in blood, as he lay struck down in battle in the midst of the kings."}},{"n":19,"text":"तं मामनार्यपुरुषं मित्रद्रुहमधार्मिकम् ।\nकिं स वक्ष्यति दुर्धर्षः समेत्य परलोकजित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What will that unconquerable one, conqueror of the other world, say to me, a base man, a traitor to friends, a man without dharma, when we meet?"}},{"n":20,"text":"जलसंधं महेष्वासं पश्य सात्यकिना हतम् ।\nमदर्थमुद्यतं शूरं प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See Jalasandha, the great bowman, struck down by Satyaki, a hero and great chariot-fighter who gave up his life for me."}},{"n":21,"text":"काम्बोजं निहतं दृष्ट्वा तथालम्बुसमेव च ।\nअन्यान्बहूंश्च सुहृदो जीवितार्थोऽद्य को मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Kamboja killed, and Alambusa too, and many other friends, what use is life to me today?"}},{"n":22,"text":"व्यायच्छन्तो हताः शूरा मदर्थे येऽपराङ्मुखाः ।\nयतमानाः परं शक्त्या विजेतुमहितान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heroes who died fighting for me, never turning their backs, striving with all strength to defeat my enemies,"}},{"n":23,"text":"तेषां गत्वाहमानृण्यमद्य शक्त्या परंतप ।\nतर्पयिष्यामि तानेव जलेन यमुनामनु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall go to them and today repay my debt as best I can, tormentor of foes, and make them offerings of water along the Yamuna."}},{"n":24,"text":"सत्यं ते प्रतिजानामि सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वर ।\nइष्टापूर्तेन च शपे वीर्येण च सुतैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I promise you truly, best of all who bear weapons, and swear by sacrifices and good works, by my strength and by my sons:"}},{"n":25,"text":"निहत्य तान्रणे सर्वान्पाञ्चालान्पाण्डवैः सह ।\nशान्तिं लब्धास्मि तेषां वा रणे गन्ता सलोकताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"that having killed all those Panchalas and the Pandavas in battle, I shall have peace, or else I shall go to their world."}},{"n":26,"text":"न हीदानीं सहाया मे परीप्सन्त्यनुपस्कृताः ।\nश्रेयो हि पाण्डून्मन्यन्ते न तथास्मान्महाभुज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Helpers of mine do not now seek my cause, for lack of care and honor; they think the Pandavas better than us, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्वयं हि मृत्युर्विहितः सत्यसंधेन संयुगे ।\nभवानुपेक्षां कुरुते सुशिष्यत्वाद्धनंजये ॥","meaning":{"en":"For death was dealt in battle by the truthful one himself; you remain indifferent because you are such a good teacher to Dhananjaya."}},{"n":28,"text":"अतो विनिहताः सर्वे येऽस्मज्जयचिकीर्षवः ।\nकर्णमेव तु पश्यामि संप्रत्यस्मज्जयैषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore all who wished to win for us have been killed. I see only Karna wishing us victory now."}},{"n":29,"text":"यो हि मित्रमविज्ञाय याथातथ्येन मन्दधीः ।\nमित्रार्थे योजयत्येनं तस्य सोऽर्थोऽवसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fool who, without knowing a friend as he truly is, sets him to work for a friend's cause, has his purpose fail."}},{"n":30,"text":"तादृग्रूपमिदं कार्यं कृतं मम सुहृद्ब्रुवैः ।\nमोहाल्लुब्धस्य पापस्य जिह्माचारैस्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such is this deed that has been done by me, the work of my friends, who said things in this manner and that, crooked in conduct, through the folly of me, a greedy sinner."}},{"n":31,"text":"हतो जयद्रथश्चैव सौमदत्तिश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nअभीषाहाः शूरसेनाः शिबयोऽथ वसातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jayadratha is killed and the brave son of Somadatta; the Abhishahas, Shurasenas, Shibis and Vasatis too."}},{"n":32,"text":"सोऽहमद्य गमिष्यामि यत्र ते पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nहता मदर्थं संग्रामे युध्यमानाः किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"So today I shall go where those bulls among men are, killed in battle for me while fighting Kiritin."}},{"n":33,"text":"न हि मे जीवितेनार्थस्तानृते पुरुषर्षभान् ।\nआचार्यः पाण्डुपुत्राणामनुजानातु नो भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have no use for life without those bulls among men. Let my teacher, the teacher of the Pandavas, give us leave.\""}}]}]}